   "text": "This drawing matches mirex (C10Cl12), so I wrote the SMILES by assigning each vertex in the image and then checking the bonds.\n\n**Atoms.** There are 12 Cl labels and 10 ring carbons. Two of the carbons are CCl2: the one at the right of the five-membered ring and the one at the centre-left. The other eight carbons each carry one Cl.\n\n**Connectivity.** Label the carbons as follows:\n- A and E are the top and bottom centre carbons.\n- B and D are the upper-right and lower-right carbons.\n- C is the right CCl2.\n- F and G are the left upper and lower carbons.\n- H is the centre-left CCl2.\n- I and J are the inner right carbons.\n\nEach carbon then has four bonds:\n- C bonds to B and D.\n- B bonds to C, F and I.\n- A bonds to F, H and I.\n- F bonds to A, B and G.\n- I bonds to A, B and J.\n- D, E, G and J are the mirror images of B, A, F and I.\n- H bonds to A and E.\n\n**Check.** Every carbon has four substituents, and the SMILES below reproduces this connectivity atom for atom. No wedges or hashes are drawn, so I included no stereochemistry.\n\nSMILES: ClC1(Cl)C2(Cl)C3(Cl)C4(Cl)C2(Cl)C5(Cl)C(Cl)(C4(Cl)Cl)C3(Cl)C15Cl"
